What you can borrow for your own design:

Fixed weekly allotments: Having a fixed “pool” of points per week (e.g., 1 M/week) gives scarcity and competition.

Snapshot windows: End-of-week cutoff windows encourage continuous participation rather than one‑time bursts.

Referral bonus: Affiliate/referral points can help virality. (e.g., 1:4 ratio in Hyperliquid)

Evolving criteria: Start with simpler rules, then widen/adjust criteria to include broader user types—for fairness and retention.

Opaque weighting: You may disclose broad criteria (volume, trades, liquidity) but keep weighting discreet to discourage gaming.

Sybil / wash‐trade prevention: Have rules to detect self‑dealing, repeated minimal trades, etc.

Inclusivity phase: As you progress, add ways for smaller users to earn (not just whales or heavy traders).

